cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI Cyber Analyst: a grounded multi-agent pipeline for network threat explanation"
message: "If you use this software or the course materials, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jansen
    given-names: Maximilian
    alias: Water6446
repository-code: "https://github.com/Water6446/U-of-U-Internship"
abstract: >-
  A four-agent LLM pipeline that investigates network flow data and explains
  what it finds: a Network Analyst that reads flows through deterministic tools,
  a Threat Intelligence agent that maps findings to MITRE ATT&CK with grounding
  enforced in code, a Kill Chain agent that builds a phase narrative and reports
  its divergence from a code-derived crosswalk, and a Report Writer that
  synthesizes the result. Ground truth is quarantined in an evaluation sidecar
  the agents never see. Includes a five-module undergraduate course and a lab.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - large-language-models
  - llm-agents
  - mitre-attack
  - intrusion-detection
  - kill-chain
  - security-education
